# HANDYMAN DEPLOY D01 — Docker build context exclusions.
#
# Everything not listed as required by the Dockerfile is kept out of the build
# context so the image cannot inherit local state, secrets, or developer
# artifacts. The Dockerfile copies only:
#   package.json, package-lock.json, tsconfig.json, src/,
#   docker/production-migrate.sh

# --- Version control ---------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitattributes
.github

# --- Dependencies and build output (both rebuilt inside the image) -----------
node_modules
dist
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo
.nyc_output

# --- Local runtime data and secrets ------------------------------------------
# .data holds the local evidence store (EVIDENCE_STORAGE_DIR); .env files hold
# local credentials. Neither may ever enter a build context or image layer.
.data
.env
.env.*

# --- Tests, docs, and repository tooling (not needed at runtime) -------------
tests
docs
scripts
*.md
.editorconfig
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
